WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.135 --> 00:00:09.058
beautiful day, two birds were sitting on a log.

2
00:00:09.699 --> 00:00:13.661
As they floated down the Nile River, they chatted away.

3
00:00:13.681 --> 00:00:16.303
"Have you caught any delicious fish?"

4
00:00:16.984 --> 00:00:17.644
asked Mrs.

5
00:00:17.724 --> 00:00:21.507
Bluewing. "Well, I almost did several times!"

6
00:00:22.107 --> 00:00:23.008
began Mrs.

7
00:00:23.068 --> 00:00:27.851
Greenfeather. She leaned closer to Mrs.

8
00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:33.363
Bluewing. "But you-know-who is lurking in the waters," she whispered.

9
00:00:33.383 --> 00:00:35.805
"You mean you mean Mrs.

10
00:00:37.006 --> 00:00:39.067
Bluewing's eyes got big.

11
00:00:39.087 --> 00:00:40.688
"That's right!

12
00:00:41.008 --> 00:00:42.609
The prince of the swamp!"

13
00:00:43.310 --> 00:00:47.573
snapped the crocodile as he leaped up from under the water.

14
00:00:48.253 --> 00:00:51.155
The poor birds nearly died of fright.

15
00:00:53.277 --> 00:00:57.300
All the animals were terrified of the great big crocodile.

16
00:00:57.884 --> 00:01:02.427
The crocodile ate whatever he wanted whenever he wanted!

17
00:01:03.148 --> 00:01:09.352
After finishing a big meal, the crocodile usually took a nap under the bushes.

18
00:01:10.032 --> 00:01:14.215
He was just about to doze off when "Ouch!"

19
00:01:15.316 --> 00:01:17.538
The crocodile opened his eyes.

20
00:01:19.319 --> 00:01:21.580
Something was causing him pain.

21
00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:26.704
"Ha-ha-ha! I'm the strongest beast on earth!"

22
00:01:27.132 --> 00:01:28.453
laughed the crocodile.

23
00:01:28.473 --> 00:01:31.374
"Nothing can cause me pain!"

24
00:01:31.914 --> 00:01:32.694
he boasted.

25
00:01:33.535 --> 00:01:38.677
The crocodile was about to go back to sleep when "Ouch!

26
00:01:38.697 --> 00:01:42.678
Ouch!" he cried out.

27
00:01:43.279 --> 00:01:45.339
The crocodile rubbed his jaw.

28
00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:48.821
The ache was coming from inside his mouth.

29
00:01:50.361 --> 00:01:56.444
When he couldn't stand the pain any longer, he decided to go to the dental clinic.

30
00:01:57.052 --> 00:02:00.073
"Help! It hurts so much!"

31
00:02:00.694 --> 00:02:02.294
the crocodile roared.

32
00:02:02.895 --> 00:02:06.876
No one expected to see the crocodile at the dental clinic!

33
00:02:07.496 --> 00:02:09.677
He had never been there before.

34
00:02:10.338 --> 00:02:13.139
The dentist was a very old bird.

35
00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:18.961
seems to be the problem?"

36
00:02:19.562 --> 00:02:22.383
he asked in a low, slow voice.

37
00:02:22.403 --> 00:02:24.744
"My teeth hurt!"

38
00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:27.301
moaned the crocodile.

39
00:02:27.321 --> 00:02:33.126
"Open your mouth and say, 'ahhh,'" the dentist instructed.

40
00:02:33.666 --> 00:02:40.251
The crocodile opened his mouth as wide as he could and said, "Ahhh!"

41
00:02:41.072 --> 00:02:44.874
The dentist's head disappeared into the crocodile's mouth.

42
00:02:44.894 --> 00:02:49.878
"How long have you had this pain?"

43
00:02:50.619 --> 00:02:52.180
he asked from inside.

44
00:02:53.184 --> 00:02:58.027
"Urhemghehmdogoeth," answered the crocodile.

45
00:02:58.047 --> 00:03:00.709
"It looks pretty bad.

46
00:03:00.729 --> 00:03:05.072
I have to go in deeper," the dentist said.

47
00:03:05.092 --> 00:03:10.015
"Urghemdogege," replied the crocodile.

48
00:03:10.035 --> 00:03:11.456
"Don't worry.

49
00:03:12.077 --> 00:03:23.656
I'll be careful," echoed the dentist.

50
00:03:23.676 --> 00:03:25.317
Suddenly there was a rumbling noise.

51
00:03:25.337 --> 00:03:26.957
It came from the crocodile's stomach!

52
00:03:26.977 --> 00:03:31.238
The crocodile was in so much pain that he had forgotten to have lunch!

53
00:03:31.258 --> 00:03:32.699
He felt very hungry.

54
00:03:32.719 --> 00:03:35.279
"Wait a minute," he thought to himself.

55
00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:38.780
"There is a bird inside my mouth!

56
00:03:39.781 --> 00:03:40.981
I can eat him!"

57
00:03:44.702 --> 00:03:48.683
finished!" the dentist suddenly shouted from inside.

58
00:03:48.703 --> 00:03:50.624
"How does it feel?"

59
00:03:51.344 --> 00:03:54.846
The dentist pulled his head out of the crocodile's mouth.

60
00:03:56.806 --> 00:03:58.147
"The pain's gone!

61
00:03:58.707 --> 00:03:59.727
It's gone!"

62
00:04:00.428 --> 00:04:02.749
the crocodile shouted with joy.

63
00:04:02.769 --> 00:04:10.552
"Unless you take care of your teeth, the pain will come back," the dentist warned him.

64
00:04:10.572 --> 00:04:15.414
"How can I take care of my teeth?"

65
00:04:16.034 --> 00:04:17.315
asked the crocodile.

66
00:04:17.335 --> 00:04:20.436
"You can't do it by yourself.

67
00:04:21.156 --> 00:04:24.559
I must clean them for you," said the dentist.

68
00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:30.765
The crocodile thought about his lunch again, but he decided not to eat the bird.

69
00:04:32.687 --> 00:04:40.173
Of course, the crocodile still eats whatever he wants, but he must go to the dentist for regular

70
00:04:40.233 --> 00:04:47.520
checkups. And he cannot eat the dentist, because if he does, who will take care of his teeth?

71
00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:51.981
The Nile crocodile is indeed the prince of the swamp.

72
00:04:53.241 --> 00:04:59.383
He will devour just about anything, but there is one bird that he won't eat.

73
00:05:00.003 --> 00:05:05.905
When the crocodile sees this bird, he comes out of the water and opens his mouth.

74
00:05:06.545 --> 00:05:12.427
Then the bird goes to work and cleans all 64 of the crocodile's teeth.

75
00:05:13.227 --> 00:05:17.852
That is how this bird got its nickname—the crocodile bird!
